{:edb/db-before-t 2860 :edb/db-after-t 2861 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536173 50 #inst "2026-10-09T18:08:47.435Z" 13194139536173 true] [17592186105822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387163 13194139536173 true] [17592186105824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387170 13194139536173 true] [17592186387163 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387164 13194139536173 true] [17592186387163 1089 "q-126744" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387163 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536173 true] [17592186387163 1100 "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1).$" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387163 1113 #uuid "36087a77-de9c-54d4-8570-665799a1fd10" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387163 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $F$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=f+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $f$ is the position vector of $F.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{FG} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,1⟩-⟨-5,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387165 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387166 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387167 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387168 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387169 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1041 "selection" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387166 13194139536173 true] [17592186387164 1110 #uuid "aac6f2cb-01c6-5596-aa8e-cd099dd99144" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387165 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536173 true] [17592186387165 1111 #uuid "7c02a6cb-8517-54ec-b552-1e1a0689cda9" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387166 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536173 true] [17592186387166 1111 #uuid "42f0a19a-07c9-50d9-9509-a712a1e685b4" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387167 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536173 true] [17592186387167 1111 #uuid "284b8741-4fde-5117-a4a6-c665c4ce6c52" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387168 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536173 true] [17592186387168 1111 #uuid "869bfa2a-6dcf-5505-871d-aa8c523516b4" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387169 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536173 true] [17592186387169 1111 #uuid "5544d965-eff4-5b3d-9f8f-bdda177aa80a" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387170 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387171 13194139536173 true] [17592186387170 1089 "q-162161" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536173 true] [17592186387170 1100 "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1,-1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ b \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387170 1113 #uuid "f673252d-f985-582f-b040-6f3a954cdf57" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387170 1145 "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+1+0=4.\n$$" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387172 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387173 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387174 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387175 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387176 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1041 "selection" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387173 13194139536173 true] [17592186387171 1110 #uuid "3dc93760-d0b0-5810-85f8-61f6441f9783" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387172 1034 "3" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536173 true] [17592186387172 1111 #uuid "66342827-5cf6-5474-a1ba-b18b10cf0657" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387173 1034 "4" 13194139536173 true] [17592186387173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045